<body><main class="wrap">
<h1>DeenWallet Transfer Privacy Policy</h1>
<small>Effective date: 24 October 2026</small>
<p>This Privacy Policy explains how DeenWallet Transfer handles information provided when you register, authenticate, verify your identity, use wallet features, contact support, or complete transactions.</p>
<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2><p>Depending on the features you use, we may collect your name, username, phone number, email address, account number, authentication and security information, transaction details, saved recipient details, notification settings, the devices and sessions you sign in with, and technical records needed to operate and secure the service. If you choose to verify your identity we also collect the identity information described in section 3.</p>
<h2>2. Why We Use Information</h2><p>We use information to create and maintain accounts, verify identity and contact details, apply the correct daily limits, authenticate users, process transactions, calculate applicable charges, send receipts and service notices, provide support, prevent fraud and unauthorized access, troubleshoot technical problems, maintain security logs, meet legal obligations, and improve the reliability of DeenWallet Transfer.</p>
<h2>3. Identity Verification (KYC) Information</h2><p>When you apply for identity verification we collect the type of document you use (National ID card, driver's licence or passport), the full name on the document, the document number, your date of birth, the expiry date where the document has one, photos of the front and, where applicable, the back of the document, and a selfie. We use this only to confirm who you are, to set your daily limit, to stop the same document being used on more than one account, and to prevent fraud and meet legal obligations. The document photos and the document number are stored encrypted, and the number is also kept as a one-way fingerprint used to detect the same document on another account. Only authorised administrators can open them, and each time a reviewer opens your details or a photo it is recorded in an audit log. We do not show your documents to other customers and we do not sell them. If a request is declined the photos are deleted immediately and you may apply again. Approved verification information is kept while your verification is active and for as long as we reasonably need it for security, dispute handling and legal obligations.</p>
<h2>4. Devices and Sign-in Sessions</h2><p>For each sign-in we keep a record so that you can see and control where your account is signed in: the type of device and app or browser, the first and most recent time it was used, and the beginning of the network address it connected from. You can see these records under Trusted Devices in the menu and remove any of them, which signs that device out. Removed and expired sessions are cleaned up automatically.</p>
<h2>5. Passwords, PINs, Biometrics and Security Data</h2><p>Passwords and PINs are stored using security controls designed to avoid storing them as readable credentials. Verification codes and security events may be retained for a limited operational period. Never share your password or PIN with support personnel. If you turn on biometric login, your fingerprint or face data stays on your Android device and is never sent to or stored by DeenWallet Transfer. We store only a public key and a device label that let your device prove it is yours.</p>
<h2>6. Transaction Information</h2><p>Transaction records may include amounts, recipient details, provider or bank information, transaction status, reference codes, timestamps, and related technical records. This information is used to complete transactions, investigate disputes, maintain accurate records, apply daily limits, and protect the service.</p>
<h2>7. Notifications</h2><p>We send service notifications by email and, if you allow them, push notifications to your device. For push notifications we keep the device notification token supplied by your phone or browser. You can turn push notifications off in your device settings, but some important emails and security notices will still be sent.</p>
<h2>8. Service Providers</h2><p>DeenWallet Transfer may rely on infrastructure, email, database, payment, bank or mobile-money service providers to deliver features. Information necessary for a requested service, such as the recipient and amount of a transfer, may be processed by those providers under their applicable terms and privacy practices.</p>
<h2>9. Sharing and Disclosure</h2><p>We do not treat your personal information as public information. We may disclose relevant information when necessary to provide requested services, protect DeenWallet Transfer and its users, investigate fraud or abuse, comply with legal obligations, or respond to lawful requests.</p>
<h2>10. Data Protection</h2><p>We use technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the service, including authentication controls, access restrictions, encrypted credential and identity document storage, security logging, audit logs for access to identity documents, and controlled administrative access. No online service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
<h2>11. Retention</h2><p>We retain account, transaction, security, and support information for as long as reasonably necessary for service delivery, security, dispute handling, legal obligations, and legitimate operational purposes. Identity documents of declined requests are deleted immediately, and sign-in session records are removed automatically after they expire.</p>
<h2>12. Your Responsibilities and Choices</h2><p>You should keep your contact details accurate and promptly report unauthorized activity. You can review and remove your signed-in devices, turn biometric login on or off, and manage notification permissions on your device. Where the system provides profile or account controls, you may update permitted information, and you may contact support about information that requires administrative assistance.</p>
<h2>13. Children</h2><p>DeenWallet Transfer is intended for users who are legally permitted to use the service. We do not knowingly design the service to collect information from children who are not permitted to register.</p>
<h2>14. Policy Changes</h2><p>We may revise this policy as DeenWallet Transfer develops or legal and security requirements change. The effective date will be updated when a new version is published.</p>
<h2>15. Contact</h2><p>For privacy, security, identity verification, account, or transaction questions, contact DeenWallet Transfer support using the support options available in the application.</p></main></body></html>
